cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use splytters in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "splytters: Embedding-based train/test splitting beyond random splits"
abstract: >-
  splytters provides train/test splitting algorithms that operate on embeddings
  with three objectives — adversarial (minimize train/test similarity, for hard
  generalization tests), overlap (maximize similarity, for sanity checks), and
  balanced (match distributions, for fair evaluation) — plus interpretable
  per-modality "sorters" and a split-quality report. It integrates with the
  scikit-learn cross-validation protocol, pandas, PyTorch, and HuggingFace
  datasets.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Larson
    given-names: Stefan
    email: stefan.larson@vanderbilt.edu
    affiliation: Vanderbilt University
version: 0.2.1
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/gxlarson/splytters"
url: "https://github.com/gxlarson/splytters"
keywords:
  - train-test-split
  - adversarial-splits
  - dataset-partitioning
  - model-evaluation
  - robustness
  - machine-learning
